  "notes": [
    "Holding registers only (functions 03, 06 and 16). The manual gives each register in hex and in decimal (hex + 1); the hex number is the wire address and is used here, address base 0.",
    "Floating-point values, 32-bit integers and ASCII text span registers with the lower-addressed register as the high half.",
    "The programmable-settings registers are only valid in the meter's settings update mode; writes to a register outside its mode return an illegal data address exception. The commands need the password (5555 when passwords are disabled).",
    "Reserved registers are left out; the 6-cycle readings block is at 900 and the 60-cycle block at 1000.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
